1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:00,950
Here is a question

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:02,850
that sounds too simple to be interesting.

3
00:00:03,770 --> 00:00:05,530
Can you measure anything on its own

4
00:00:05,570 --> 00:00:06,710
without having a reference?

5
00:00:07,330 --> 00:00:10,030
A distance, a temperature, intelligence?

6
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:12,870
Hold on to that question,

7
00:00:12,910 --> 00:00:15,610
because if we follow it honestly step by step,

8
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:17,970
it takes us somewhere I did not expect.

9
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:21,030
Say you are standing ten metres away from me.

10
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:22,270
I am the starting point,

11
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:23,950
the zero on the tape.

12
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:25,450
Now walk over to me,

13
00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:26,570
hand me the tape,

14
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:29,290
and measure the same gap from where you stand.

15
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:31,090
Same distance, different reference.

16
00:00:31,710 --> 00:00:33,730
Nothing is measured absolutely.

17
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:35,210
Every number we ever write down

18
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:37,830
quietly carries a second piece of information:

19
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:39,310
the place it was measured from.
